# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Do not commit .env.
#
# EARTHDATA_TOKEN and FIRMS_MAP_KEY can instead be saved for the user with
# `/key earthdata user` and `/key firms user` (files under ~/.atlas/keys).
# `/key earthdata session` and `/key firms session` keep a value in memory
# until Atlas exits. The session value wins. Those commands do not print the
# value and do not write it into this checkout.
#
#
# Agent (required to run the LLM loop)
# Create a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# NASA Earthdata login (required for the FLDAS training-table extract and for downloads from
# modis_*, viirs_vnp09ga, gedi, icesat2_atl03, and smap_l3; CMR search is public)
# Register, then generate a token. The token lasts 60 days, and an account can hold two.
# 1. Open https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov and choose Register. Activate the account from
#    the email NASA sends. Log in.
# 2. On your profile, open Generate Token, click Generate Token, then Show Token.
#    Guide: https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/documentation/for_users/user_token
# 3. Paste the token below.
# 4. Approve the two applications this download uses. A 403 means one of them
#    is still missing. Open Applications → Authorized Apps → Approve More
#    Applications, then search for and approve each of these:
#      - Hyrax in the cloud
#      - NASA GESDISC DATA ARCHIVE
#    Accept the NASA GESDISC DATA ARCHIVE license when it is shown.
# EARTHDATA_TOKEN is used when set. Otherwise the username and password are sent as
# basic auth. A ~/.netrc entry for urs.earthdata.nasa.gov is used when none of these are set.
# MODIS, VIIRS, GEDI, ICESat-2, and SMAP downloads use EARTHDATA_TOKEN only, sent as a
# bearer token to https hosts under nasa.gov. A 401 on those downloads means the token is
# unset or expired.
EARTHDATA_TOKEN=
EARTHDATA_USERNAME=
EARTHDATA_PASSWORD=

# NASA FIRMS active-fire search (required for firms_viirs and the other FIRMS sources)
# 1. Open https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/map_key/
# 2. Request a free MAP_KEY with your email (NASA emails the key)
# 3. Paste it below. Check remaining quota on that same page ("Check status").
# Limit: 5,000 transactions per 10 minutes. Suomi-NPP FIRMS products end 2026-11-01;
# prefer firms_viirs_noaa20 / firms_viirs_noaa21 after that.
FIRMS_MAP_KEY=

# Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem (CDSE) login (required to download the cdse_* sources:
# Sentinel-3 OLCI/SLSTR/SRAL, Sentinel-5P NO2/CH4/CO, CLMS burnt area). Search is public.
# 1. Open https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/ and choose Login, then Register. Confirm the
#    account from the email CDSE sends.
# 2. Put the account email in CDSE_USERNAME and its password in CDSE_PASSWORD. Wrap the
#    password in single quotes if it contains #, spaces, or quotes: CDSE_PASSWORD='p#ss'
# 3. Run a pull, e.g. atlas data sentinel5p atmosphere --date 2026-06-01:2026-06-10
#    --coords -71.19,42.04,-70.92,42.22 --limit 1
# Atlas exchanges this pair for a 30-minute access token at identity.dataspace.copernicus.eu
# and sends the token only to download.dataspace.copernicus.eu. No CDSE S3 keys are needed.
# A wrong pair fails each download with HTTP 401 from the identity service. CDSE has no
# /key command: set it here or in the environment. Values are never printed.
CDSE_USERNAME=
CDSE_PASSWORD=

# The API Key required to use the rsicc tool. Getting an API key is generally free
# To get one go to https://aistudio.google.com/api-keys and click "Create API Key".
# The Gemini client is an optional extra: uv sync --extra gemini
# GeoTIFF inputs also need rasterio: uv sync --extra gemini --extra geotiff
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Models rsicc_tool uses. The first answer comes from ATLAS_RSICC_MODEL
# (default gemini-3.5-flash-lite). A low-confidence or flagged answer is retried once on
# ATLAS_RSICC_FALLBACK_MODEL (default gemini-3.6-flash). The agent may only pick one of
# these two. Model codes: https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models
ATLAS_RSICC_MODEL=
ATLAS_RSICC_FALLBACK_MODEL=
